      "@id": "https://doi.org/10.24432/C5689X",
      "@type": "dcat:Dataset",
      "dct:title": "Heterogeneity Activity Recognition",
      "dct:description": "HHAR contains motion-sensor time series from heterogeneous smartphones and smartwatches. The activity experiment records accelerometer and gyroscope measurements for nine users performing biking, sitting, standing, walking, stair up and stair down. A separate still experiment records stationary devices in six orientations. The complete UCI download includes Activity recognition exp.zip and Still exp.zip. Activity-recognition CSVs contain timestamps, x/y/z measurements, user, model, device and ground-truth activity information; the source documents a null ground-truth class and missing values. The dataset supports research on activity recognition and sensor heterogeneity. Source documentation: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/344/heterogeneity+activity+recognition .",
